  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Procedure vs In Re : Madhusudan Dolai on 22 August, 2017 Author: Joymalya Bagchi Bench: Joymalya Bagchi 1 22.08.2017 sdas C.R.R. No. 685 of 2017 In Re : An application under Section 482 of the Code of Criminal Procedure.",
    "facts": "Prosecution case against the petitioner is to the effect that the petitioner and other accused persons were dealing and/or selling spurious liquor and due to consumption of such liquor one Abhijit Manna and Amitava Karan expired. In conclusion of investigation, charge- sheet was filed under Sections 272/273/328/304/120B of the Indian Penal Code, under Section 46AA of the Bengal Excise Act and 16(3) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act against the petitioner and other accused persons.",
    "arguments": "Learned Counsel appearing for the petitioner submits that viscera report of the deceased Abhijit Manna showed that no poison was detected in the viscera of the deceased. Relying on such report, prayer was made to discharge the petitioner from the aforesaid case. Such prayer being turned down the petitioner is before this Court. Learned Counsel appearing for the State submits that opinion of the autopsy surgeon in the post-mortem report is that the victim Abhijit Manna had died due to unknown poisoning. That apart, large quantity of illicit liquor was seized from the possession of the petitioner and other accused persons and chemical examination of seized liquor showed that it was spurious and unfit for human consumption. Hence, the petitioner ought not to be discharged from the instant case.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned Counsel appearing for the petitioner submits that viscera report of the deceased Abhijit Manna showed that no poison was detected in the viscera of the deceased. Relying on such report, prayer was made to discharge the petitioner from the aforesaid case. Such prayer being turned down the petitioner is before this Court. Learned Counsel appearing for the State submits that opinion of the autopsy surgeon in the post-mortem report is that the victim Abhijit Manna had died due to unknown poisoning.",
    "respondent_arguments": "That apart, large quantity of illicit liquor was seized from the possession of the petitioner and other accused persons and chemical examination of seized liquor showed that it was spurious and unfit for human consumption. Hence, the petitioner ought not to be discharged from the instant case.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
